From 08feb26e5be0c3a3b7bff61cd393f56ba7ae793e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 10:47:50 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: mt7996: keep the BSS TX power over a regulatory
 change

__mt7996_init_txpower() raises phy->txpower to the maximum power of the
band. On a regulatory change after a BSS set its TX power,
mt7996_regd_notifier() runs it again, and the SKU limits then ignore the
TX power of the BSS until mac80211 reports it again.

Leave phy->txpower to the BSS. Since commit 9b06eef07184 ("wifi: mt76:
mt7996: limit the SKU TX power to the current channel"), a scan or an
offchannel operation before a BSS sets its TX power gets the maximum
power of the current channel without it.

Fixes: 959a2d40007f ("wifi: mt76: mt7996: initialize phy txpower")
Signed-off-by: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
---
 mt7996/init.c | 1 -
 1 file changed, 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/mt7996/init.c b/mt7996/init.c
index ab2de70f1..2574d1390 100644
--- a/mt7996/init.c
+++ b/mt7996/init.c
@@ -376,7 +376,6 @@ static void __mt7996_init_txpower(struct mt7996_phy *phy,
 		target_power = DIV_ROUND_UP(target_power, 2);
 		chan->max_power = min_t(int, chan->max_reg_power,
 					target_power);
-		phy->txpower = max(phy->txpower, chan->max_power);
 		chan->orig_mpwr = target_power;
 	}
 }
